WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.511
Where are we going to get the wealth

00:00:01.511 --> 00:00:03.793
to build the&nbsp;types of 
business that we want.

00:00:03.793 --> 00:00:06.288
And the answer is going to have
 to be cooperative economics.

00:00:07.074 --> 00:00:10.051
There's&nbsp;a lot of different 
versions of cooperativism.

00:00:10.051 --> 00:00:12.615
What I'm talking about
today is worker&nbsp;ownership.

00:00:12.615 --> 00:00:14.105
Right now, today,

00:00:14.105 --> 00:00:15.172
in South Bronx,

00:00:15.172 --> 00:00:18.073
is the country's largest 
worker-owned company.

00:00:18.073 --> 00:00:20.976
And it was founded by black 
and Latinx home&nbsp;care workers

00:00:20.976 --> 00:00:24.029
who are now able to pay 
themselves living wages,

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:27.156
they have full-time&nbsp;hours, they 
have benefits and a pension,

00:00:27.156 --> 00:00:29.642
through their membership as a unit of SEIU.

00:00:29.642 --> 00:00:32.595
And these women owners now 
receive a dividend back

00:00:32.595 --> 00:00:35.465
on their ownership every year that 
the&nbsp;company has been profitable,

00:00:35.465 --> 00:00:37.207
which has been most years.

00:00:37.207 --> 00:00:38.757
They don't have any big investors.

00:00:38.757 --> 00:00:41.551
They don't have&nbsp;fat-cat CEOs
 or absentee owners

00:00:41.551 --> 00:00:43.450
taking the profit out of the company.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.794
They each pay in about 1,000&nbsp;dollars over time

00:00:47.794 --> 00:00:49.778
in order to gain ownership,

00:00:49.778 --> 00:00:51.074
and now they own their job.

00:00:51.074 --> 00:00:53.558
I'm so inspired by&nbsp;what they're doing,

00:00:53.558 --> 00:00:56.145
because it really represents an alternative

00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:57.959
to the type of economy&nbsp;we have now,

00:00:57.959 --> 00:00:59.476
which exploits all of us.

